#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:384
#: 4b176921c1154f39ba405113462bf251
msgid "Using a Power Distribution Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:389
#: 20f16fb2863e4f4089b4b9f47f2108c9
msgid "There are two methods of connecting the motor outputs.  Either connect the electronic speed controllers (ESCs) directly to the autopilot OR use a power distribution board (PDB)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:392
#: 1a366800875e4077bf600e9920b0fee1
msgid "When using a PDB, connect the power (+), ground (-), and signal (s) wires for each ESC to the PDB according to motor number. Find your frame type below to determine the assigned order of the motors. Then connect the signal wires from the PDB to the main output signal pins on the autopilot  (ensuring that the motor order numbers match the main output pin numbers on the controller). If you are using a power module, it is optional to connect the power and ground wires from the PDB to the autopilot board. If you would like to use these cables in addition to or instead of the power module or as a common point for low current servos, connect the ground (-) wire to a main output ground (-) pin and the power (+) wire to a main output power (+) pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:405
#: 4761f976998d426a9f2cb07d159ac561
msgid "KDE (and other) Opto Isolated ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:407
#: 97f32ad114da48d9ae79fafc852f9fb6
msgid "The KDEXF-UAS and KDEF-UASHV Series are opto-isolated and do not provide BEC power output for the peripheral equipment. They require +5V to power the opto-isolator and while the Pixhawk can be powered from the servo rail, it does not provide +5V to the servo rail. The ESCs must be powered by a BEC or with a jumper from an unused connector on the board. It is strongly recommended that you use a BEC to power the rail rather than a jumper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:418
#: e02091920b934b9eb206c160102f0265
msgid "The KDE ESCs have fixed PWM ranges so you must manually set the output range of each PWM signal so that RCx_MIN is 1100 and RCx_MAX is 1900us using the Advanced Parameter or Full Parameter Settings Page in the planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:424
#: 68e6b192838d493c859e8bc4b3718095
msgid "Pixhawk ESC issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:426
#: 28c25aabd24047248a266b015f295470
msgid "Some ESCs have been reported as not working with Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:428
#: 02cdc0874b554a0c9dfbcfe2c134e927
msgid "The Pixhawk should work with every ESC that works with a normal RC receiver (because it sends the same type of signal) but there is `one known exception, the EMAX ESC <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/2094>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:431
#: 27e747088e8e4062b16a07c3132c6d47
msgid "In most cases problems are due to incorrect wiring. Always connect signal and ground. Check your ESC type to decide how to connect the +5V line. For Pixhawk you must connect both the signal and the signal ground in order to make the ESC work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connect-escs-and-motors.rst:435
#: a69422b25f364aa6ba5b417cc3ce7406
msgid "For more information see `this video <https://youtu.be/6C1YG1e2aTo>`__."
msgstr ""
